;; What the model reads of each tool brainyard/memory.clj defines: its description,
;; by tool id (brainyard.tool-words, byj-2e8.5). Read by the model, so a
;; resource (RFC-001).
{"memory$history"
  "Search what this project was ASKED and ANSWERED in earlier sessions. Use it before re-deriving something that sounds like it has been worked out before, or to find how a question was answered last time. This is a record of turns, not of decisions — memory$recall is where the decisions are."
 "memory$recall"
  "Search durable memory — what was learned in earlier sessions and written down. Reach for it when a question sounds like it has been settled before, or when you are about to assume something about this project you cannot see in front of you. Nothing is recalled automatically; this is the only way memory enters a turn."
 "memory$read"
  "Read one memory in full by its key, after memory$recall named it."
 "memory$remember"
  "Write something down for a later session: a decision and why, a constraint that is not in the code, a dead end worth not repeating. Not a summary of what you just did — the transcript already has that, and a memory nobody needs is a memory in everyone's way."
 ;; arguments, as "<tool> :arg", and result fields, as "<tool> result :field" (byj-2e8.9)
 "memory$history :query"
  "Key nouns; every word of 3+ characters must appear."
 "memory$history :limit"
  "Turns to return (default 5)."
 "memory$history result"
  "newest first; :when is how long ago, :question and :answer clipped"
 "memory$recall :query"
  "What you are looking for. How it matches is the store's business, not this tool's: a single distinctive word usually finds more than a phrase, so if a query comes back empty, try one word from it."
 "memory$recall result"
  ":memories is the store's own output"
 "memory$read :key"
  "The key memory$recall reported."
 "memory$remember :content"
  "The insight, in a sentence or two, written for someone who was not here."
 "memory$remember :key"
  "A slug naming its topic, as a person would search for it (deploy-freeze, staging-db-port); generated from the content otherwise. A later turn is told the key and the first line of a memory its question matches, so make the first line say the point."
 "memory$remember result"
  ":stored is the store's own output"}
